{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" are the kept vertices in the base’s order, at view indices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view keeps two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and renumbered with one array load per entry and no hashing. A spanning subgraph keeps every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex at its base index."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges"}]},{"text":" keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are, and, if an edge set was given,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when it is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices: an edge’s index is its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rank among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a count per 64-bit word, so the rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices: building","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its edge mask would cost O(m). One on every vertex keeps the base’s rows, edge indices and flat","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rows.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The view holds a copy of the base (value semantics), so mutating the original never shows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through. Phase 1 needs a base with vertex indices; a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" with vertex holes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps at construction."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","title":"SubgraphView","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV","modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SubgraphView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView.swift#L29"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"code":"subgraph_view","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"code":"AsSubgraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SubDigraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"code":"filtered_graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"]},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"references":{"doc://GraphOperations/s9EscapableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Escapable"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations":{"title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph-implementations","abstract":[]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/base":{"title":"base","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"base","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/base","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The graph the view filters.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/DirectedEdges":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedEdges","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"DirectedEdges","ki